    "reuse_rule": "Prefer verified saved URLs. Otherwise inspect direct children of the configured parent for matching title, marker and account. Reuse exactly one complete match; report multiple matches. A same-name object missing its marker or saved URL may be a partial creation: reconcile only if identifiable as this run/project; otherwise report ambiguity and do not create another. Apply the same rule to databases.",
    "creation_recovery": "After an uncertain create response or failed marker/URL persistence, re-query the parent before any further create. Inspect same-name incomplete candidates. Resume only an object identifiable as this run/project; otherwise stop that creation as ambiguous. Serialize setup runs.",
    "views_fallback": "If linked views are unsupported, create equivalent views in source databases and link those databases from the dashboard. Report actual created views."
  },
  "rules": {
    "account_identity": "Use a stable account ID if available; otherwise use a canonical profile URL. Keep the chosen format stable across runs; do not silently switch.",
    "media_identity": "Use a stable media ID or canonical unique post URL without query or fragment. Do not match by title or date.",
    "observation_date": "Actual timestamp converted to Asia/Seoul, formatted YYYY-MM-DD. Never backdate a later observation.",
    "period": "Preserve exact source boundaries and timezone. Do not round timestamp boundaries to dates. Use a fixed lifetime scope token for cumulative metrics. For unconfirmed scope, include the original source scope label in a stable unknown-scope token to avoid collisions between different unknown periods; retain the original label in notes. Use the literal unknown timezone token when source timezone is unconfirmed.",
    "numbers": "Exact observed nonnegative counts only. Unavailable or unreadable values are null with a reason. Abbreviated values remain text notes. Zero requires a real observed zero.",
    "deduplication": "Query exact key before writing: no match creates, one match updates, multiple matches report conflict. Serialize writes because Notion has no assumed uniqueness constraint.",
    "history_updates": "Update only successfully collected values and their timestamps. Document retained older values with their original collection timestamp in notes.",
    "latest_snapshot": "Promote one verified lifetime observation group only after history readback. All applicable metrics must be checked: exact values and source-confirmed unsupported nulls are complete; unknown, unreadable or abbreviated applicable values block promotion. Promote only if not older than the stored group. Set 최신 지표 상태 to 검증 중 before updates and 검증 완료 only after successful readback. Hide unverified groups from latest-performance views.",
    "account_period": "Followers use their own snapshot timestamp. Views and reach use the specified period; split observations if their periods differ. Do not sum rolling reach or media reach into account reach.",
    "secrets": "Real account identifiers, page URLs, exports and runtime reports stay outside public source files. Authentication belongs in supported connection settings.",
    "key_serialization": "Serialize key_components as a JSON array of actual values in exactly the listed order, with JSON null for missing boundaries. Use stable canonical string representations and JSON null, not ad-hoc delimiter concatenation."
  },
